<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kambula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kambula was fought on 29 March 1879 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a>, when a British column under Colonel Evelyn Wood, defending a fortified camp in north-western Zululand, repulsed a major attack by the main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> army. The heavy Zulu losses made it a turning point of the war after the disaster at Isandlwana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kambula.jpg" alt="Battle of Kambula" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Robinson, after Melton Prior (1845 - 1910) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kambula_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
